      "writtenOn": "2010-12-16T07:19:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason the temporary fail causes are listed is because operators often want to be able to list which fail causes in their network shall override the fail causes default set as permanent. The operators are more interested to customize the temporary failure causes than the permanent ones.\n\nAnother solution could be to make the permanent fail causes customizable since this list will be sort of an inverse of the temporary one. Anyhow, it will then be a slightly more complex procedure customizing the fail causes since the obvious permanent fail causes must first be listed, then making sure the requested temporary fail causes are not within the permanent fail cause list.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAA+X///8Y\u003d",
      "revId": "7bffc01dfa544593922ff8fab6046f5207be5f4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
